The attached image is relevant.
The attached image, corresponding to Figure 4 from the PDF (Journal of Controlled Release 204 (2015) 51-59, page 5), displays confocal microscopy images illustrating the uptake of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red), FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA, green), and their complex by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). The top row shows Nano-11 uptake, the middle row shows minimal soluble OVA uptake, and the bottom row demonstrates significantly enhanced uptake of OVA when adsorbed to Nano-11, with clear intracellular co-localization of both nanoparticles and antigen. This indicates Nano-11's efficacy in improving antigen delivery to dendritic cells, a critical mechanism for its adjuvant properties.